message.content:
Below is a minimal, self‑contained example of a “rotating card” that flips (or rotates) when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the HTML and CSS into your own file or into an online editor such as CodePen / JSFiddle.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body{
  display:flex;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  min-height:100vh;
  margin:0;
  background:#f0f0f0;
  font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card{
  width:260px;
  height:360px;
  perspective:800px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card inner wrapper (the part that actually rotates) ---------- */
.card-inner{
  width:100%;
  height:100%;
  position:relative;
  transition:transform 0.8s ease;
  transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front & back faces ---------- */
.card-front,
.card-back{
  position:absolute;
  width:100%;
  height:100%;
  backface-visibility:hidden;   /* hide the back side when facing away */
  border-radius:12px;
  overflow:hidden;
  box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.card-front{
  background:#fff;
  display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;
  padding:20px;
  text-align:center;
}

.card-back{
  background:#333;
  color:#fff;
  transform:rotateY(180deg);    /* start rotated so it's hidden */
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;
  padding:20px;
  text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner{
  transform:rotateY(180deg);    /* flip the card on hover */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
  <div class="card-inner">
    <!-- Front face -->
    <div class="card-front">
      <h2>Front Side</h2>
      <p>Some brief description or image.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Back face -->
    <div class="card-back">
      <h2>Back Side</h2>
      <p>More details, links, or a call‑to‑action.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | The page is centered and given a light gray background. |
| **2** | `.card` sets the *perspective* – this is what creates the 3‑D depth effect. |
| **3** | `.card-inner` is the element that will rotate. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps its children in 3‑D space. |
| **4** | Two faces (`.card-front` and `.card-back`) are positioned absolutely on top of each other. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the back side when it’s turned away. The back face starts rotated 180° so it’s initially hidden. |
| **5** | On hover, the inner wrapper rotates 180°, flipping the card. |

Feel free to tweak the rotation axis (`rotateY`, `rotateX`, or even `rotateZ`), the duration, or add more styling (images, gradients, etc.) to suit your design. Happy coding!
